A||||2||Fformula88||Need help with '88 Rear Disk Brakes||||5||
Z||000000||Fformula88||03-15-2000||09:30 AM||||I am having a horrible time figuring out these rear brakes on my 88 Formula.  I can get the shoes out, and I can rotate the piston, but it doesn't go back into the caliper.  I cannot seem to bottom it out.  The parking brake mechanism is disconnected, and it seems like everything should be fine.  It just doesn't go back in (yep, I took the cover off the fluid resevoir too).  Did I miss a step maybe?  Or is the Caliper shot?  Any advice is greatly appreciated.  Thanx.||||reg||5
Z||000002||TheFiero64||03-15-2000||05:06 PM||||I had the same problem when I was doing my brakes on my 88. I used a c clamp and squeezed the piston with it and turned the piston with large pliers. It finally turned in. I haven't had anymore problems with it.<BR>Hope this works for you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Josh||||reg||3
Z||000003||zebrex||03-15-2000||11:23 PM||||WOw I just went through the exact same thing friday on my 88 formula. However I am sad to admit I let the calipers get the best of me and I went to advance auto parts and ordered a new set for 75 each (75 core also) When I got them one of the banjo bolt holes had a helicoil in it so I took it back and ordered another one. I finally put the rears on but then I broke a bleeder screw on one of the front ones while bleeding the system, so I ordered another one It should be here friday or monday or... To make a long story not so long I hope you have better luck than I did.||||reg||1
